<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSES.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Close of play scores on the first</p>
<p>day of four-day English County Championship cricket matches on</p>
<p>Wednesday:</p>
<p>At Cardiff: Hampshire 94-1 (M.Hayden 54 not out) v</p>
<p>Glamorgan.</p>
<p>At Old Trafford: Northamptonshire 281-4 (K.Curran 91 not</p>
<p>out, R.Bailey 58) v Lancashire.</p>
<p>At Trent Bridge: Derbyshire 283-5 (D.Jones 71 not out,</p>
<p>V.Clarke 50) v Nottinghamshire.</p>
<p>At Taunton: Yorkshire 52-3 v Somerset.</p>
<p>At Horsham: Kent 245 (T.Ward 76; K.Newell 4-61). Sussex</p>
<p>102-4.</p>
<p>No play possible in the following matches due to rain - At</p>
<p>Chester-le-Street: Durham v Worcestershire, at Edgbaston:</p>
<p>Warwickshire v Middlesex, at Leicester: Leicestershire v Surrey,</p>
<p>at Gloucester: Gloucestershire v Essex.</p>
</text>
